Case 4: case 1 behind an inner join on n1; expect c = 1, 2     

===================================================
a    b    c    
1     2     1     
1     1     2     

Query plan:
temp(order by)
    subplan: nl-join (left outer join)
                 outer: idx-join (inner join)
                            outer: iscan
                                       class: n? node[?]
                                       index: i_n? term[?] (covers)
                                       cost:  ? card ?
                            inner: iscan
                                       class: p? node[?]
                                       index: i_p? term[?] (covers)
                                       cost:  ? card ?
                            cost:  ? card ?
                 inner: sscan
                            class: m? node[?]
                            sargs: term[?]
                            cost:  ? card ?
                 during:term[?]
                 cost:  ? card ?
    sort:  ? asc, ? asc
    cost:  ? card ?
Query stmt:
select /*+ ORDERED USE_NL */ n?.a, n?.b, n?.c from n? n? inner join p? p? on p?.a=n?.a left outer join m? m? on n?.b= ?:?  where (n?.a> ?:? ) order by ?, ?
